  "releaseNotes": "PDChat Voice Mode: the microphone no longer hears the assistant read an answer aloud when it was waiting for the wake phrase or paused in Dictate mode, as it did when the question was typed. Whatever is heard while an answer is read aloud is never typed or sent, and a microphone that was waiting for the wake phrase waits for it again afterwards. IChatService gains InterruptPhrases, off by default and with a default implementation so other implementers still compile: when set, saying one of the phrases, such as Merlin, while an answer is read aloud stops it and starts listening, while every other word heard meanwhile is ignored. An answer that itself says one of the phrases is read with the microphone paused, so it cannot interrupt itself. An answer that replaces one still being read no longer hands the microphone back early. PDFileExplorer: NavigateToItemAsync opens the folder holding a file or folder and selects it, loading that folder's contents once, where NavigateToAsync opens each folder on the way in turn; it returns false, with the deepest folder found open, when the item is not there. Without its toolbar the explorer's panes now take the full height. Given an ExceptionHandler, PDFileExplorer and PDTree pass a failure in any of their event handlers to it instead of ending the Blazor circuit; without one, a failure is thrown as before. PDTree gains LoadChildNodesAsync and PDTable gains ScrollItemIntoViewAsync, and a failing PageChanged or PageSizeChanged handler on PDTable is passed to its ExceptionHandler.",
